# ============================================================================
# Not the file you want — see .env.local.example
# ============================================================================
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local.example` is the single source of truth for this project's
# environment variables. It lists every variable the code actually reads, says
# which are required, and flags the two that are easy to get dangerously wrong
# (the Supabase project ref, and the Resend sending domain).
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why this file is now a pointer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It used to be a 150-line template, and most of it was aspirational. It
# documented OPENROUTER_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_MODEL, DATABASE_URL, NEXTAUTH_SECRET,
# JWT_SECRET, SESSION_MAX_AGE, SESSION_INACTIVITY_TIMEOUT,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIN_SITE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_*, DEBUG, SMTP_*, QUICKBOOKS_*,
# TWILIO_* and NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID -- none of which appear anywhere in
# the codebase. It also omitted SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY's sibling secrets that
# the app does read.
#
# Two example files that disagreed meant a new developer could spend an afternoon
# provisioning an OpenRouter key for a chatbot that does not exist, and still hit
# a missing-variable error on first run. One file, checked against the code, is
# better than two that are each half right.
#
# If a variable listed above is genuinely wanted later, add it when the code that
# reads it lands -- not before.
#
# ============================================================================
